{
  "note": "The two contract files (piece 5C, procedure 2.8): the Solusi contract file (Excel, every Monday; row 1 field names, row 2 labels) and the ServiceNow contract report (ast_contract). They are matched by the Solusi contract number, which ServiceNow keeps in Vendor contract. Procurement owns the data: a wrong value is corrected in Solusi, because the next import writes over ServiceNow. The problems of the contract data ('problems') are split over two cards: For Procurement raises the problems of Solusi itself, Contracts to fix in ServiceNow the ones SACM corrects in ServiceNow ('change' and 'set' are the words of its fix list). An inactive contract owner or Procurement partner: when the loaded reports know an active account with the same name, the upload picked the wrong account and SACM sets the active one ('ownerInactive', 'partnerInactive'); when they know none, the person left and Procurement names a new person in Solusi ('ownerLeft', 'partnerLeft').",
